## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Agents and sessions
  status: planned

  req F-1.1:
    when: an agent is created
    then: it is one `Agent` durable object, which receives external events, runs no inference, and
          delegates work to its `SessionProcess`es

  req F-1.2:
    when: a session holds work
    then: the tasks are in the session's task list; a thread has no task list of its own

  req F-1.3:
    when: a session is part of an agent
    then: the session has its own `SessionProcess`, feed and task list, and inherits the agent's
          permissions

  req F-1.4:
    when: a session is created with no agent
    then: it runs as a standalone session

  req F-1.5:
    when: a session that is part of an agent is created
    then: its home space is either the current space or, when the agent has an identity, the
          agent's home space; nothing assumes one of the two [Q-2]
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Intra-agent delegation
  status: planned

  req F-2.1:
    when: a session delegates a task to a thread
    then: the thread runs in the same session and process, and works from the session's task list

  req F-2.2:
    when: an agent delegates a task to another of its sessions
    then: the task runs in that session's own `SessionProcess` and is recorded in its task list

  req F-2.3:
    when: work is delegated to a thread or to a session of the same agent
    then: `AgentService` handles it
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Cross-agent delegation
  status: planned

  req F-3.1:
    when: an agent looks for another agent
    then: it finds it through HALO contacts, which return ECHO objects of type actor (people or
          agents) for the members of the spaces they share

  req F-3.2:
    when: work is delegated to another agent
    then: `AgentService` handles it

  req F-3.3:
    when: an agent delegates to another agent in the base case
    then: it sends a durable message to the other agent's `Agent` object

  req F-3.4:
    when: an agent delegates a tracked task to another agent
    then: it sends a reference to the task, and the task is assigned to the other agent
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Agent addressing
  status: planned

  req F-4.1:
    when: an agent is referenced
    then: it is addressed by its DID, as a URI inside ECHO

  req F-4.2:
    when: an agent is created without an identity
    then: it still gets a generated DID

  req F-4.3:
    when: several agents are in one space
    then: each has its own DID and they co-exist in that space
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Per-space memory
  status: planned

  req F-5.1:
    when: a session in a space reads or writes memory
    then: it uses that space's `MemoryService`, whether or not the session belongs to an agent

  req F-5.2:
    when: several agents are in one space
    then: they share that space's memory
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Discord
  status: planned

  req F-6.1:
    when: an agent interacts with Discord
    then: it goes through `DiscordService`
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Agent identity and personal space
  status: planned
  desc: The eventual goal; [F-4.2] and [F-5.2] are the interim state.

  req F-7.1:
    when: an agent is created
    then: it has its own identity and its own personal space
```

```mdl
feat F-8: Agent picker in the prompt input
  status: planned

  req F-8.1:
    when: the user opens the prompt input
    then: it offers a selection of agents, with "Composer" always listed and "Claude Code" listed
          when plugin-claude is installed

  req F-8.2:
    when: the user selects "Composer"
    then: the prompt runs in an agent-less (standalone) session [F-1.4]

  req F-8.3:
    when: custom agents exist
    then: each appears in the same selection, and selecting one runs the prompt with that agent
```

```mdl
feat F-9: Current process
  status: planned
  desc: |
    `Process.current: Effect<Process.Process, NoCurrentProcessError, Process.ManagerService>`
    returns the process the calling code runs in.

  req F-9.1:
    when: code running inside a process yields `Process.current`
    then: it gets that process's `Process.Process`, read from the ambient `Process.ManagerService`

  req F-9.2:
    when: code with a `Process.ManagerService` that is not scoped to a process yields
          `Process.current`
    then: it fails with `NoCurrentProcessError`
```

```mdl
feat F-10: Delegation entry points
  status: planned

  req F-10.1:
    when: work is delegated at any tier
    then: an operation starts it, and the operation goes through `AgentService`

  req F-10.2:
    when: the delegation strategy spawns a sub-agent, or the thread scheduler starts a thread
    then: it does so through `AgentService`, not by spawning or scheduling directly

  req F-10.3:
    when: an operation needs a new process for agent work
    then: it asks `AgentService`; it never calls `Process.spawn` or `Process.ManagerService.spawn`
          itself

  req F-10.4:
    when: a model delegates to a thread
    then: it calls operations (today's `thread_delegate` and `thread_wait` tools), which go through
          `AgentService`
```

```mdl
feat F-11: Session object
  status: planned

  req F-11.1:
    when: code refers to the ECHO type that a session runs on
    then: it is named `Session`; the name `Chat` is gone

  req F-11.2:
    when: a `Session` object is stored
    then: its DXN stays `org.dxos.type.assistant.chat`, and the type definition carries a TODO to
          rename the DXN later

  req F-11.3:
    when: a `Session` object is run
    then: a `SessionProcess` runs it

  req F-11.4:
    when: an `Agent` object is run
    then: an `AgentProcess` runs it, in the agent's `Agent` durable object
```

```mdl
feat F-12: Session annotation on processes
  status: planned

  req F-12.1:
    when: a process is spawned on behalf of a session
    then: it carries a session annotation whose value is the URI of that `Session` object

  req F-12.2:
    when: a process with a session annotation spawns a child
    then: the child carries the same session annotation unless the spawn names another session

  req F-12.3:
    when: code needs the session it runs for
    then: it reads the session annotation of `Process.current` [F-9]

  req F-12.4:
    when: a process is spawned on behalf of an agent
    then: it carries an agent annotation whose value is the URI of that `Agent` object, and a
          spawned child inherits it

  req F-12.5:
    when: a `SessionProcess` spawns a process for a thread's tool call or code execution
    then: the new process carries a thread annotation whose value is that thread's id, beside the
          session annotation, and a spawned child inherits it
```

```mdl
feat F-13: AgentService
  status: planned
  desc: |
    The one service for agent work. It is a global singleton, not scoped to a process or a
    conversation.

  req F-13.1:
    when: code creates, finds or runs an agent or a session
    then: it goes through `AgentService`, which manages both

  req F-13.2:
    when: code yields `AgentService.currentSession`
    then: it gets the `Session` named by the session annotation of `Process.current`, and fails
          with `NoCurrentSessionError` when there is none

  req F-13.3:
    when: code yields `AgentService.currentAgent`
    then: it gets the `Agent` named by the agent annotation of `Process.current`, or none for a
          standalone session

  req F-13.4:
    when: code needs to find other agents or sessions
    then: `AgentService` discovers them from the annotations of the processes it manages

  req F-13.5:
    when: code uses `HarnessService`
    then: the service is deprecated; each of its reads and control verbs has an `AgentService`
          replacement scoped by `currentSession`

  req F-13.6:
    when: code yields `AgentService.currentThread`
    then: it gets the thread named by the thread annotation of `Process.current`, or none for
          work on the session's main thread
```

```mdl
feat F-14: Agent module
  status: planned
  desc: |
    `@dxos/compute` holds one namespace module, `Agent`, for the agent types and the service.
    `AgentService` elsewhere in this spec is `Agent.Service`.

  req F-14.1:
    when: code refers to the agent types or the service
    then: it uses `Agent.Agent` (the ECHO `Agent` type), `Agent.Session` (the ECHO `Session` type,
          formerly `Chat`) and `Agent.Service`, all from `@dxos/compute`

  req F-14.2:
    when: the types move from `@dxos/assistant`
    then: `Agent.Agent` moves without the helpers that need `@dxos/assistant` (the context binder)

  req F-14.3:
    when: code acts on a session (submits a prompt, reads or adds context, waits, terminates,
          subscribes to its trace)
    then: it calls a standalone verb on the `Agent` module that takes the `Agent.Session` as its
          first argument; there is no session handle with methods
```

```mdl
feat F-15: Choosing the receiver
  status: planned
  desc: The criteria are still in flux.

  req F-15.1:
    when: work is delegated
    then: the model decides whether a thread, another session of the agent, or another agent
          receives it

  req F-15.2:
    when: the model delegates part of the same work-stream to run in parallel
    then: it delegates to a thread

  req F-15.3:
    when: the model delegates a separate work-stream
    then: it delegates to another session

  req F-15.4:
    when: the model delegates to another agent
    then: it does so only because that agent's permissions or specialization are needed
```

## QA

```mdl
test QA-1: An agent hands a change it may not make to an agent that may
  desc: The scripted story `stories-assistant/agents/Delegation` (CrmAgents) walked by a person. Scout and Ledger share
    one CRM tool that requires `/crm/write`; only Ledger is granted it. Scout is refused, hands the request to Ledger,
    and Ledger makes the change on its own permissions.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-3.2, F-3.3, F-15.4]
  status: draft
  given:
    - the story `stories/stories-assistant/agents/Delegation` CrmAgents, with the `crmAgents` scripted model
  steps:
    - name: See who holds what
      do: Hover Scout's name above its chat, then Ledger's.
      expect: Scout holds no permissions; Ledger holds Change CRM records
    - name: Read the process tree
      do: Look at the process tree under the object tree.
      expect: Ledger's session lists /crm/write and Scout's lists no permissions
    - name: Ask Scout for the change
      do: Click the chip "Bramble Coffee Roasters signed the contract. Mark them active in the CRM." in Scout's chat.
      expect: Scout's call to set the status is denied, and the run reads "1 denied"
    - name: Watch the hand-over
      do: Wait.
      expect: Scout hands the request to Ledger, whose chat shows it as context rather than as a user message, and
        Ledger reports the account active
    - name: Check the account
      do: Click Bramble Coffee Roasters in the object tree.
      expect: its record shows status active
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Agent, Session and Thread are the three tiers of agent work: Agent is identity and access, Session is the durable worker with its own feed and task list, Thread is a microtask inside a session.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
  source: https://preview.composer.space/w/BPBG3HN4O2XTMB5MRDZQXJBAXA7LAH4IA/object/01M879PMFK98ARXFN9FVSKM01B
```

```mdl
decision D-2: An agent has one main durable object that receives external events, runs no inference and delegates to sessions; it has a home space for memory, ECHO database, access tokens and skills. Attached sessions inherit the agent's permissions, and standalone sessions stay supported.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-1.3, F-1.4]
  source: https://preview.composer.space/w/BPBG3HN4O2XTMB5MRDZQXJBAXA7LAH4IA/object/01M879PMFK98ARXFN9FVSKM01B
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Delegation has an intra-agent scope (sessions and threads of one agent) and a cross-agent scope (separate identities, spaces and entry points).
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2, F-3]
  source: https://preview.composer.space/w/BPBG3HN4O2XTMB5MRDZQXJBAXA7LAH4IA/object/01M879PMFK98ARXFN9FVSKM01B
```

```mdl
decision D-4: Cross-agent delegation is push-based: a durable message to the other agent's main durable object, optionally with a task object in a shared space assigned to that agent. Agents find each other through HALO contacts in shared spaces and are addressed by DID.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3]
  source: https://preview.composer.space/w/BPBG3HN4O2XTMB5MRDZQXJBAXA7LAH4IA/object/01M879PMFK98ARXFN9FVSKM01B
```

```mdl
decision D-5: The task list in the project or session is the control plane; ephemeral messages (wake, start, stop) sit on top of it.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2, F-3]
  source: https://preview.composer.space/w/BPBG3HN4O2XTMB5MRDZQXJBAXA7LAH4IA/object/01M879PMFK98ARXFN9FVSKM01B
