```mdl
decision D-22: Add `Process.current: Effect<Process.Process, ..., Process.Manager>`, which returns the current process.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-9]
```

```mdl
decision D-23: `Process.current` fails with a typed `NoCurrentProcessError` when the ambient manager is not scoped to a process, and `Process.Manager` in [D-22] is the `Process.ManagerService` tag. Fills in [D-22].
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-9.1, F-9.2]
  why: The process's own `ManagerService` already knows its process (it defaults `parentProcessId` to it), but a manager built outside any process has none, and callers need to tell that case apart.
  rejected: Dying instead of failing, since being outside a process is a normal state for app-level code.
```

```mdl
decision D-24: Delegation is handled by different operations, but each eventually goes through either `AgentService` or `HarnessService`.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-10.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-25: The sub-agent spawns of the delegation strategy and the thread scheduler's threads count as delegation, so they also go through `AgentService` or `HarnessService`. Fills in [D-24].
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-10.2]
  why: Both start work in another process or thread on the agent's behalf, but today they reach `Process.spawn` and the thread lanes directly, outside both services.
```

```mdl
question Q-4: How do `AgentService` and `HarnessService` relate to the intra-agent and cross-agent delegation services of [D-13]?
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.3, F-3.2, F-10]
  context: D-13 names two delegation services split by scope, while D-24 routes all delegation through two existing services split by role (session manager, in-session control surface).
  options:
    - By tier: `HarnessService` handles threads, `AgentService` handles sessions and, later, other agents; the two delegation services sit behind them.
    - Layered: the intra-agent and cross-agent delegation services are new, and `AgentService` / `HarnessService` call into them.
    - Same: the two delegation services are `AgentService` and `HarnessService`, renamed.
```

```mdl
decision D-26: The ECHO type `Chat` is renamed to `Session`. Its DXN does not change for now; a TODO marks it for a later rename.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-11.1, F-11.2]
```

```mdl
decision D-27: A `Session` object maps to a `SessionProcess`, and an `Agent` object maps to an `AgentProcess`.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-11.3, F-11.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-28: A process has an annotation for its current session.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-12.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-29: The `AgentProcess` of [D-27] runs inside the agent's `Agent` durable object of [D-10]; it is a new process, distinct from today's `AgentProcess`, which becomes `SessionProcess`. Fills in [D-27].
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-11.4]
  why: D-10 renames today's `AgentProcess` to `SessionProcess`, so the name is free for the process that runs an `Agent` object.
```

```mdl
decision D-30: The session annotation holds the `Session` object's URI, a spawned child inherits it, and code reads it from `Process.current`. Fills in [D-28].
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-12.1, F-12.2, F-12.3]
  why: Tools and sub-agents run as child processes of the session's process, so inheriting the annotation lets them find their session without the harness-host lookup `HarnessService` does today.
  rejected: Reusing `Process.TargetAnnotation`, because a child's target is the object it works on, not the session it works for.
```

```mdl
decision D-31: `HarnessService` is deprecated.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-13.5]
```

```mdl
decision D-32: `AgentService` is extended to manage agents and sessions.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-13.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-33: `AgentService` is a global singleton. It exposes `AgentService.currentAgent` and `AgentService.currentSession`, which query the current process and discover the others through annotations.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-13.2, F-13.3, F-13.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-34: Operations do not spawn processes directly; they go through `AgentService`.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-10.3]
```

```mdl
decision D-35: With `HarnessService` deprecated, every delegation path in F-10 goes through `AgentService` alone, and `HarnessService`'s reads and control verbs move to `AgentService`, scoped by `currentSession`. Supersedes [D-25] and fills in [D-31] to [D-34].
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  supersedes: D-25
  affects: [F-10.1, F-10.2, F-13.5]
  why: D-24 names two services and D-31 deprecates one of them, so the routing rule keeps only the other.
```

```mdl
decision D-36: `currentSession` fails with `NoCurrentSessionError` outside a session; `currentAgent` returns none for a standalone session instead of failing. A process run for an agent carries an agent annotation, inherited like the session annotation. Fills in [D-33].
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-12.4, F-13.2, F-13.3]
  why: A standalone session is normal (F-1.4), so having no agent is a value; having no session means the caller is outside agent work. `currentAgent` needs an annotation to read, as `currentSession` has one in F-12.
```

```mdl
decision D-37: Thread delegation (today's `thread_delegate` and `thread_wait` tools) becomes operations that go through `AgentService`. Fills in [D-24] and [D-34].
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-10.4]
  why: Light threads are delegation started by plain toolkit tools that bypass operations, which D-24 does not allow.
  rejected: Exempting the thread tier from F-10, which leaves thread delegation unguarded and invisible to the operation catalog.
```

```mdl
decision D-38: `AgentService.currentThread` returns the current thread. Whenever a `SessionProcess` makes a tool call or runs code for a thread, it annotates the new process with that thread.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-12.5, F-13.6]
```

```mdl
decision D-39: The thread annotation holds the thread's id and sits beside the session annotation; a spawned child inherits it; `currentThread` returns none for work on the session's main thread. Fills in [D-38].
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-12.5, F-13.6]
  why: Main has no thread id in the trajectory, so a tool call made on main has no thread to name, and a tool's own child processes still work for the thread that called it.
```

```mdl
decision D-40: Q-2 stays open. A session that is part of an agent may live in the current space or, when the agent has an identity, in the agent's home space, and the design expects both.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.5]
```

```mdl
decision D-41: The ECHO types `Chat` (becoming `Session`) and `Agent` move from `@dxos/assistant` to `@dxos/compute`; `Agent` moves without its helpers. They live in one module with `Agent.Agent`, `Agent.Session` and `Agent.Service`, and the methods of the `AgentService.Session` handle become standalone verbs that take an `Agent.Session` as their first argument.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-14]
```

```mdl
decision D-42: "Without helpers" means the helpers that need the context binder of `@dxos/assistant` (`makeInitialized`, `resetChatHistory`); the helpers that need only ECHO move with the type, and `getFromChatContext` gives way to `currentAgent`. Fills in [D-41].
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-14.2]
  why: The binder is what keeps those two in `@dxos/assistant`; the ECHO-only helpers have no such dependency, and `getFromChatContext` reads `HarnessService`, which D-31 deprecates.
```

```mdl
decision D-43: There are no separate intra-agent and cross-agent delegation services: `AgentService` handles all delegation, and may later hold permissions for the different kinds of delegation.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  supersedes: D-13
  answers: Q-4
  affects: [F-2.3, F-3.2]
```


```mdl
decision D-44: The model decides which receiver delegated work goes to: threads for light parallelisation of the same work-stream, sessions for separate work-streams, and agents only when another agent is needed (for permissions, specialization, etc.). These criteria are still in flux.
  date: 2026-11-24
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-15]
```

```mdl
decision D-45: The first cut of cross-agent delegation finds the receiver by name among the agents in the caller's space, not through HALO contacts, and hands the message to that agent's primary session as a turn whose sender is the calling agent, with its text marked synthetic so the chat shows it as context rather than as the reader's words. The receiving session runs on its own agent's authority, which `AgentService` takes from its `defaultAuthority` option when the open names none; the caller's authority never reaches it.
  date: 2026-11-26
  by: agent:claude-opus-5-5
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.1, F-3.2, F-3.3]
```

```mdl
decision D-46: QA-1 walks cross-agent delegation in the `agents/Delegation` story: two agents with different permissions, one refused and handing the change to the other, with each agent's and each process's permissions shown along the way.
  date: 2026-11-26
  by: agent:claude-opus-5-5
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.2, F-3.3, F-15.4]
```
